[281.102147, "i", "cat > FIX_SUMMARY.md << 'EOF'\n# Release Tooling Fixes\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n### 1. Version Bump Priority Bug (semver.py)\n**Problem**: The bump_version() function processed commit tags sequentially, returning on the first match. This meant tag order affected the version bump type, violating the priority rule (major > minor > patch).\n\n**Example**: ['SECURITY', 'FEATURE'] would return patch bump (2.3.2) instead of minor bump (2.4.0)\n\n**Fix**: Rewrote bump_version() to check ALL tags at each priority level before moving to the next:\n- First check if ANY tag triggers major bump\n- Then check if ANY tag triggers minor bump  \n- Finally check if ANY tag triggers patch bump\n\n**Result**: Tag order no longer matters; highest priority always wins.\n\n### 2. Changelog Section Mismatch Bug (changelog.py)\n**Problem**: The utils.py config loader normalized all dictionary keys to lowercase ('security', 'features'), but generate_changelog_entry() used a hardcoded section_order list with mixed case ('Security', 'Features'). This cause"]
[281.102281, "i", "d section keys to never match, resulting in missing or misplaced changelog entries.\n\n**Example**: Security commits were missing from changelog or defaulted to 'Features'\n\n**Fix**: \n- Updated get_section_for_tag() to return lowercase section keys\n- Added section_display_names mapping for proper capitalization\n- Updated section_order to use lowercase keys matching the config\n\n**Result**: Commits now appear under correct sections with proper formatting.\n\n## Verification\nBoth fixes tested and verified:\n- SECURITY tag correctly bumps 2.3.1 -> 2.3.2 (patch)\n- Security commits appear under 'Security' section in CHANGELOG.md\n- Priority handling works correctly for mixed tags\nEOF\n"]
[281.102332, "o", "cat > FIX_SUMMARY.md << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[281.102388, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[281.102438, "o", "# Release Tooling Fixes\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[281.102474, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[281.10251, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[281.102556, "o", "## Issues Fixed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[281.102585, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[281.102614, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[281.102662, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
